I did not add the `http-client` import. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority and grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`. Importing `http-client` would give the component an authority its declared grant doesn't include, so the grant would need to change in the graph definition first. The request also has a second problem: `PublishedDigest` has no text field, so there is no "input's text" to put in the URL. Below is the node within its declared grant. If the platform team's approval is recorded in the grant configuration, send the updated `with` clause and the field to enrich from, and I'll add the fetch. Any URL built from the input would also need percent-encoding, since `considered` ids come from the feed side.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        for id in published.considered.iter() {
            let key = format!("seen:{}", id);
            state_rw::put(&key, "1");
            recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

